    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d100">

                <pb facs="0162" n="154" xml:id="pg154"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/7288: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in Spain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Barcelona</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-01-31T11:00:00+00:00">January 31, 1938—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 3—9:11 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>870. An official statement places the number of deaths from yesterday’s air raids
                    at 150 as of last night. Unofficial estimates place them at twice that
                    figure.</p>
                <p>The statement also asserts that the Government’s offer to desist from raids in
                    cities in the far rear guard, quoted in my 867, January 29, 10 a.m.,<anchor
                        n="11" xml:id="d100-f1"/> has been rejected by a speaker over the Salamanca
                    radio.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
